  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 3e4b5683c1ea36345958694d590b6436, type: 3}
  m_Name: COC3_Quiz_LO2_NetworkServices_Q01
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::QuizQuestionData
  questionText: Why must a server use a static IP address instead of taking one from
    DHCP?
  choices:
  - Static addresses are faster than leased ones
  - Clients and services find the server by an address that must never change
  - DHCP cannot issue addresses to server operating systems
  - A static address uses less bandwidth
  correctChoiceIndex: 1
  points: 10
  explanation: A lease can change. Every client, every DNS record and every mapped
    drive that points at this machine would break when it did.
